+<p>The implementation has two main components:</p>
+<p><strong><code>runWithRetry(taskDef, taskResults, maxRetries = 3)</code></strong> — Wraps a single task fn with retry logic. On failure, it catches the error and retries up to <code>maxRetries</code> times with exponential backoff (100ms → 200ms → 400ms, capped at 1s). If all attempts fail, it throws a <code>PipelineError</code>.</p>
+<p><strong><code>pipeline(tasks)</code></strong> — The orchestrator. It:
+1. <strong>Validates</strong> the task list — checks for duplicates, unknown dependencies, and circular dependencies (via DFS with a recursion stack).
+2. <strong>Executes in waves</strong> — at each iteration, finds all tasks whose dependencies are satisfied (<code>getReadyTasks()</code>), launches them concurrently via <code>Promise.allSettled</code>, and collects results. Tasks that fail are tracked; if any task fails, downstream tasks are identified and the pipeline aborts with a clear error.</p>
+<p>Key decisions:
+- <strong>Wave-based parallelism</strong>: all ready tasks run simultaneously in each wave, maximizing throughput for independent work.
+- <strong>Error propagation</strong>: a failed task blocks its dependents. If any downstream tasks become unreachable (or the failed task has no dependents), the pipeline throws immediately rather than hanging.
+- <strong>Retry is per-task</strong>: each async function gets its own retry loop with backoff, isolated from other tasks.</p></div><div class='evidence'><h2>Evidence &amp; signatures</h2><pre>All **31 tests pass**, covering:
