+<p>The parser consists of three classes:</p>
+<p><strong><code>Lexer</code></strong> — Tokenizes input into a stream of tokens (<code>INT</code>, <code>FLOAT</code>, <code>STRING</code>, <code>BOOL</code>, <code>NULL</code>, <code>IDENTIFIER</code>, operators, brackets, etc.). Handles:
+- Skip whitespace and comments (<code>//</code> line, <code>/* block */</code>)
+- Read integers (<code>42</code>) and floats (<code>3.14</code>)
+- Read strings with escape sequences (<code>"hello\nworld"</code>, <code>'single'</code>)
+- Read identifiers and keywords (<code>true</code>, <code>false</code>, <code>null</code>, <code>fooBar</code>)
+- Two-character operators (<code>==</code>, <code>!=</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;=</code>, <code>&amp;&amp;</code>, <code>||</code>)
+- Friendly error messages for <code>=</code> (suggest <code>==</code>) and single <code>&amp;</code>/<code>|</code> (suggest <code>&amp;&amp;</code>/<code>||</code>)
